); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,Store at –20°C. | Storage Conditions: | Store at –20°C. Do not store in a frost-free freezer. | Storage Buffer:,,,Store at –20°C. | Storage Conditions: | Store at –20°C. Do not store in a frost-free freezer. | Storage Buffer:,Store at –20°C. | Storage Conditions: | Store at –20°C. Do not store in a frost-free freezer. | Storage Buffer:,1,storage,"Page 1 [unclassified]: Unit Definition: One unit is the amount of enzyme required to completely degrade 1 μg DNA in 10 min at 37°C, and is equivalent to (temperature: 37°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Incubate at 37°C for 30 min. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Incubate at 37°C for 15 min. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Incubate at 37°C for 15–30 min. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Some protocols suggest heating at 75°C for 5 min to inactivate DNase I [5]. (temperature: 75°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: A 10-minute incubation at 75°C (temperature: 75°C)",PDF,https://assets.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/certificate/Certificates+of+Analysis/1409038_AM2224.pdf
