Part 5,alkaline phosphatase,P09923,WHO,"Containing color-coded (green) phosphate buffer | containing sodium chloride, detergent, bovine protein | stabilizers and 0.3% chloroacetamide (CAA) as | labelled with alkaline phosphatase in Tris buffer | containing bovine stabilizers, detergent and 0.01% | Containing color-coded (blue) Tris buffer containing",,"Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. Phosphate salts commonly help control pH and contribute ionic strength; exact effects depend on pH, concentration, and other ingredients. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. A detergent/surfactant may reduce surface adsorption or aggregation in some formulations; the exact purpose and compatibility depend on the specific ingredient and concentration. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Containing color-coded (green) phosphate buffer | containing sodium chloride, detergent, bovine protein | stabilizers and 0.3% chloroacetamide (CAA) as | labelled with alkaline phosphatase in Tris buffer | containing bovine stabilizers, detergent and 0.01% | Containing color-coded (blue) Tris buffer containing",2 - 8 °C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (2 - 8 °C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,For storage of developed strips | Storage: | The test kit should be stored at 2 - 8 °C.,,,For storage of developed strips | Storage: | The test kit should be stored at 2 - 8 °C.,For storage of developed strips | Storage: | The test kit should be stored at 2 - 8 °C.,2,storage,,PDF,https://extranet.who.int/prequal/sites/default/files/whopr_files/PQDx_0202-073-00_INNO-LIA_v2.pdf
