HRP Anti-Bovine Serum Albumin antibody (ab7637),bovine serum albumin BSA,,Abcam,"Blocking Buffer : 5% BLOTTO in TBS. | Anti-BOVINE ALBUMIN (RABBIT) Antibody is an IgG fraction antibody purified from monospecific antiserum by a multi-step process which includes delipidation, salt fractionation and ion exchange chromatography followed by extensive dialysis against the buffer. | Storage buffer | Preservative: 0.01% Gentamicin sulphate Constituents: 1% Polyethylene glycol, 0.88% Sodium chloride, 0.424% Potassium phosphate solution",,"Phosphate salts commonly help control pH and contribute ionic strength; exact effects depend on pH, concentration, and other ingredients. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Blocking Buffer : 5% BLOTTO in TBS. | Anti-BOVINE ALBUMIN (RABBIT) Antibody is an IgG fraction antibody purified from monospecific antiserum by a multi-step process which includes delipidation, salt fractionation and ion exchange chromatography followed by extensive dialysis against the buffer. | Storage buffer | Preservative: 0.01% Gentamicin sulphate Constituents: 1% Polyethylene glycol, 0.88% Sodium chloride, 0.424% Potassium phosphate solution",+4°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (+4°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,Appropriate long-term storage conditions,Properties and storage information | Storage buffer | Appropriate short-term storage conditions | Appropriate long-term storage conditions | Storage information | Store in the dark,,,"Properties and storage information
