Native Carbamylated Bovine Serum Albumin protein (ab172196),bovine serum albumin BSA,,Abcam,"Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 - 7.4 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 50% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.88% Sodium chloride, 0.015% EDTA | storage-buffer | style",7.2,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Sodium azide is commonly used as a preservative to limit microbial growth. It is hazardous and can affect downstream applications; follow the product safety sheet and assay compatibility guidance. EDTA chelates metal ions. This may matter if the protein requires metal cofactors or if metal-catalyzed reactions are relevant. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 - 7.4 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 50% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.88% Sodium chloride, 0.015% EDTA | storage-buffer | style",-20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (-20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,Appropriate long-term storage conditions,Storage buffer | storage-buffer | Properties and storage information | Appropriate short-term storage conditions | Appropriate long-term storage conditions | Aliquoting information | Storage information,,Aliquoting information | Avoid freeze / thaw cycle,"Storage buffer
