ors or if metal-catalyzed reactions are relevant. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","12.1.3 Buffers and reagents .................................................................................................. 121 | • Hand washbasins, with running water, should be provided in each laboratory | 1. Diphtheria antitoxin, usually supplied in vials reconstituted at 1000 IU/ml; | visually, add 200 µl of binding buffer | 4. Incubate further at 70°C for 10 minutes | 1. Suspend single colonies in 200 µl of phosphate buffered saline (PBS) buffer | and 15 µl of a lysozyme solution (10 mg/ml in Tris-HCl, pH 8.0) | 3. Add 200 µl of binding buffer and 40 µl of a proteinase K solution (20 mg/ml) | The modified version is based on a ready-to-use mixture containing buffer, MgCl2, | 1. Weigh 3 g of agarose and add to 100 ml of 1x Tris-Borate EDTA (TBE) buffer in | 4. Place the gel tray in the electrophoresis tank containing TBE buffer pH 8.2. | Table A8. TBE 5x buffer pH 8.0 | Buffer | TE 1x pH 8.0 | Sequencing buffer | 1.75 µl | into a common dilution buffer, are then added to the wells. A calibration curve is | 12.1.3 Buffers and reagents | 1M HEPES buffer | • | If MTT dye is used for staining viable cells, extraction buffer is prepared with solution | Add 100 μl of extraction buffer to all wells and return the microplate to the 37°C",4-8°C; -20°C to -80°C; 4°C; -20°C; 6-8°C; 70°C; -25°C; 2-8°C,Cold chain indicated,Explicit refrigerated or frozen-storage wording appears in the storage evidence.,"APPENDIX 3 Long-term storage of strains ......................................................................... 78 | 2) Long-term: cryopreservation/freezing at –20°C to –80°C in glycerol broth | very selective, 