Anti-EGF antibody [EPR19173] - BSA and Azide free (ab240283),epidermal growth factor EGF,A4F3R6,Abcam,"This data was developed using the same antibody clone in a different buffer formulation containing PBS, BSA, glycerol, and sodium azide ( | Related conjugates and formulations (1) | { ""title"": ""Reactivity Data"", ""filters"": { ""stats"": ["""", ""Species"", ""Dilution Info"", ""Notes""], ""tabs"": { ""all-applications"": {""fullname"" : ""All Applications"", ""shortname"": ""All Applications""}, ""WB"" : {""fullname"" : ""Western blot"", ""shortname"":""WB""}, ""IHCFr"" : {""fullname"" : ""Immunohistochemistry (Frozen sections)"", ""shortname"":""IHC-Fr""}, ""IHCP"" : {""fullname"" : ""Immunohistochemistry (Formalin/PFA-fixed paraffin-embedded sections)"", ""shortname"":""IHC-P""} }, ""product-promise"": { ""all"": ""all"", ""testedAndGuaranteed"": ""tested"", ""guaranteed"": ""expected"", ""predicted"": ""predicted"", ""notRecommended"": ""not-recommended"" } }, ""values"": { ""Mouse"": { ""WB-species-checked"": ""guaranteed"", ""WB-species-dilution-info"": """", ""WB-species-notes"": ""<p></p>"", ""IHCFr-species-checked"": ""testedAndGuaranteed"", ""IHCFr-species-dilution-info"": """", ""IHCFr-species-notes"": ""<p>Antigen retrieval: Heated citrate solution (10mM citrate PH 6.0 + 0.05% Tween-20)</p>"", ""IHCP-species-checked"": ""testedAndGuaranteed"", ""IHCP-species-dilution-info"": """", ""IHCP-species-notes"": ""<p>(Antigen Retrieval Buffer (100X Tris-EDTA Buffer, pH 9.0) (&lt;em data-test=\""product-code\""&gt;<a href='/en-us/products/buffers/antigen-retrieval-buffer-100x-tris-edta-buffer-ph-90-ab93684'>ab93684</a>&lt;/em&gt;))</p>"" }, ""Rat"": { ""WB-species-checked"": ""guaranteed"", ""WB-species-dilution-info"": """", ""WB-species-notes"": ""<p></p>"", ""IHCFr-species-checked"": ""predicted"", ""IHCFr-species-dilution-info"": """", ""IHCFr-species-notes"": """", ""IHCP-species-checked"": ""predicted"", ""IHCP-species-dilution-info"": """", ""IHCP-species-notes"": """" } } } | Our carrier-free antibodies are typically supplied in a PBS-only formulation, purified and free of BSA, sodium azide and glycerol. This conjugation-ready format is designed for use with fluorochromes, metal isotopes, oligonucleotides, and enzymes, which makes them ideal for antibody labelling, functional and cell-based assays, flow-based assays (e.g. mass cytometry) and Multiplex Imaging applications. | Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 - 7.4 Constituents: PBS",6.0; 9.0; 7.2,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium azide is commonly used as a preservative to limit microbial growth. It is hazardous and can affect downstream applications; follow the product safety sheet and assay compatibility guidance. EDTA chelates metal ions. This may matter if the protein requires metal cofactors or if metal-catalyzed reactions are relevant. A detergent/surfactant may reduce surface adsorption or aggregation in some formulations; the exact purpose and compatibility depend on the specific ingredient and concentration. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","This data was developed using the same antibody clone in a different buffer formulation containing PBS, BSA, glycerol, and sodium azide ( | Related conjugates and formulations (1) | { ""title"": ""Reactivity Dat