How should I solubilize and store peptides?
Dissolve peptides in an appropriate buffer (acidic peptides in basic buffer and basic peptides in acidic buffer), and if necessary, sonicate briefly. Peptides containing Trp, Met, or Cys require special care to avoid oxidation, so oxygen-free water or reducing agents may be used. For storage, peptide solutions should be aliquoted and kept frozen at -20
