Human G-CSF Recombinant Protein,granulocyte colony-stimulating factor G-CSF,,Thermo Fisher,"Reconstitution: We recommend that the vial be briefly centrifuged prior to opening to bring the contents to the bottom. Lyophilized hG-CSF should be reconstituted in sterile deionized water to 0.1-1.0 mg/mL to regain full activity. These stock solutions should be apportioned into working aliquots and stored at ≤-20°C. Further dilutions should be made in low endotoxin medium or buffered solution with FBS or tissue culture grade BSA. Storage: Lyophilized Hg-CSF should be stored at 2°C to 8°C, preferably desiccated. Store reconstituted hG-CSF at ≤-20°C (not in a frost-free freezer). Keep freeze-thaw cycles to a minimum.",,"Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Reconstitution: We recommend that the vial be briefly centrifuged prior to opening to bring the contents to the bottom. Lyophilized hG-CSF should be reconstituted in sterile deionized water to 0.1-1.0 mg/mL to regain full activity. These stock solutions should be apportioned into working aliquots and stored at ≤-20°C. Further dilutions should be made in low endotoxin medium or buffered solution with FBS or tissue culture grade BSA. Storage: Lyophilized Hg-CSF should be stored at 2°C to 8°C, preferably desiccated. Store reconstituted hG-CSF at ≤-20°C (not in a frost-free freezer). Keep freeze-thaw cycles to a minimum.",4°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (4°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,Storage conditions,,,"Storage conditions
