Anti-GFP antibody [EPR14104-89] (ab183735),green fluorescent protein GFP,A0A5J6CYR6,Abcam,"Related conjugates and formulations (1) | Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 40% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.05% BSA",7.2,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium azide is commonly used as a preservative to limit microbial growth. It is hazardous and can affect downstream applications; follow the product safety sheet and assay compatibility guidance. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Related conjugates and formulations (1) | Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 40% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.05% BSA",+4°C; -20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (+4°C; -20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,Appropriate long-term storage conditions | Noncoding RNA circBtnl1 suppresses self-renewal of intestinal stem cells via disruption of Atf4 mRNA stability.,Properties and storage information | Storage buffer | Appropriate short-term storage duration | Appropriate short-term storage conditions | Appropriate long-term storage conditions | Aliquoting information | Storage information,,Aliquoting information | Avoid freeze / thaw cycle,"Properties and storage information
