Human Growth Hormone Recombinant Protein,human growth hormone,Q4R6M1,Thermo Fisher,"Storage buffer | PBS with 1mg mannitol, 1mg glycine",,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. The reported sugar/polyol may act as a stabilizer or bulking agent and can help protect proteins during freezing or drying, depending on formulation and process. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Storage buffer | PBS with 1mg mannitol, 1mg glycine",-20°C; -20° C; 4° C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (-20°C; -20° C; 4° C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,"Store lyophilized product desiccated at -20° C. Upon reconstitution, store at 4° C for 2-7 days or aliquot and store at -20° C. For long term storage add either HSA or BSA to 0.1%. Avoid repeated freeze/thaw cycles.","100 µg/mL once reconstituted | Storage buffer | Storage conditions | Store lyophilized product desiccated at -20° C. Upon reconstitution, store at 4° C for 2-7 days or aliquot and store at -20° C. For long term storage add either HSA or BSA to 0.1%. Avoid repeated freeze/thaw cycles.",100 µg/mL once reconstituted | Reconstitute using distilled water to a concentration not less than 100 µg/mL.,"-20°C, Avoid Freeze/Thaw Cycles | Store lyophilized product desiccated at -20° C. Upon reconstitution, store at 4° C for 2-7 days or aliquot and store at -20° C. For long term storage add either HSA or BSA to 0.1%. Avoid repeated freeze/thaw cycles.","100 µg/mL once reconstituted
