Frequently asked questions (FAQs)
What is the molecular weight of insulin in Insulin, human recombinant, zinc solution (Cat. No. 12585014)?
The molecular weight of insulin in Insulin, human recombinant, zinc solution (Cat. No. 12585014) is 5807.7 g/mol.
Find additional tips, troubleshooting help, and resources within our
How should I store Insulin, human recombinant, zinc solution? Should I aliquot it as a best storage practice or are multiple freeze/thaw cycles okay?
As a general precaution, we suggest making useable aliquots at the time of thawing and freezing the unused aliquots back at -5 to -20 degrees C. We do not recommend multiple freeze/thaw cycles for this product as we have not done extensive testing in this regard.
