Anti-IL-6 antibody [EPR23819-103] (ab290735),interleukin 6 IL-6,,Abcam,"Heat mediated antigen retrieval with Tris-EDTA buffer (pH 9.0, epitope retrieval solution 2) for 20 mins | Heat mediated antigen retrieval with Tris-EDTA buffer (pH 9.0, epitope retrieval solution2) for 20 mins | Blocking and diluting buffer and concentration : 5% NFDM/TBST. The expression of IL-10 is upregulated in response to LPS in treated RAW 264.7 (PMID : 23012430, 15218058) but not in non-differentiated NIH/3T3 cells. In western blot, anti-IL-6 antibody (ab290735) staining at 1/1000 dilution. Anti-GAPDH antibody ( | Blocking buffer and concentration : | Diluting buffer and concentration : | Blocking / Dilution buffer and concentration : 5% NFDM/TBST. | Related conjugates and formulations (1) | Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 - 7.4 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 40% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.05% BSA",9.0; 7.2,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium azide is commonly used as a preservative to limit microbial growth. It is hazardous and can affect downstream applications; follow the product safety sheet and assay compatibility guidance. EDTA chelates metal ions. This may matter if the protein requires metal cofactors or if metal-catalyzed reactions are relevant. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Heat mediated antigen retrieval with Tris-EDTA buffer (pH 9.0, epitope retrieval solution 2) for 20 mins | Heat mediated antigen retrieval with Tris-EDTA buffer (pH 9.0, epitope retrieval solution2) for 20 mins | Blocking and diluting buffer and concentration : 5% NFDM/TBST. The expression of IL-10 is upregulated in response to LPS in treated RAW 264.7 (PMID : 23012430, 15218058) but not in non-differentiated NIH/3T3 cells. In western blot, anti-IL-6 antibody (ab290735) staining at 1/1000 dilution. Anti-GAPDH antibody ( | Blocking buffer and concentration : | Diluting buffer and concentration : | Blocking / Dilution buffer and concentration : 5% NFDM/TBST. | Related conjugates and formulations (1) | Storage buffer | pH: 7.2 - 7.4 Preservative: 0.01% Sodium azide Constituents: PBS, 40% Glycerol (glycerin, glycerine), 0.05% BSA",+4°C; -20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (+4°C; -20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,Appropriate long-term storage conditions,Properties and storage information | Storage buffer | Appropriate short-term storage duration | Appropriate short-term storage conditions | Appropriate long-term storage conditions | Aliquoting information | Storage information,,Aliquoting information | Avoid freeze / thaw cycle,"Properties and storage information
