Lysozyme Recombinant Rabbit Monoclonal Antibody (ST50-02),lysozyme,O75951,Thermo Fisher,"Storage buffer | TBS, pH 7.4, with 40% Glycerol, 0.05% BSA | Recombinant rabbit monoclonal antibodies are produced using in vitro expression systems. The expression systems are developed by cloning in the specific antibody DNA sequences from immunoreactive rabbits. Then, individual clones are screened to select the best candidates for production. The advantages of using recombinant rabbit monoclonal antibodies include: better specificity and sensitivity, lot-to-lot consistency, animal origin-free formulations, and broader immunoreactivity to diverse targets due to larger rabbit immune repertoire.",7.4,"Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Storage buffer | TBS, pH 7.4, with 40% Glycerol, 0.05% BSA | Recombinant rabbit monoclonal antibodies are produced using in vitro expression systems. The expression systems are developed by cloning in the specific antibody DNA sequences from immunoreactive rabbits. Then, individual clones are screened to select the best candidates for production. The advantages of using recombinant rabbit monoclonal antibodies include: better specificity and sensitivity, lot-to-lot consistency, animal origin-free formulations, and broader immunoreactivity to diverse targets due to larger rabbit immune repertoire.",4°C; -20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (4°C; -20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,"Store at 4°C short term. For long term storage, store at -20°C, avoiding freeze/thaw cycles.","Stora