Lysozyme Solution (50 mg/mL),lysozyme,O75951,Thermo Fisher,"Add 1-2 µL of 50 mg/mL Lysozyme Solution (Cat. No. 90082) to 200 µL of the EasyPep lysis buffer provided in the kit and proceed with the sample prep. Add 200 µL of the prepared lysis solution to 5 X 10E8 bacterial cells (E. coli cells) (OD600 equal to 1, corresponding to 1 X 10E8 CFUs). Lyse by pipetting the sample repeatedly and centrifuge at 16,000 x g for 5 mins. Alternatively, E. coli cells can be lysed in lysis buffer using bead beating or sonication instead of lysozyme. After lysis, dilute samples to 1 mg/mL using lysis buffer, proceed with the EasyPep protocol for reduction, alkylation, digestion, and clean up as described in the product manual.",,"The source reports a buffer/formulation, but its ingredients are not recognized by this simple interpretation rule set. Use the exact composition, pH, concentrations, and manufacturer's technical notes to interpret it. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Add 1-2 µL of 50 mg/mL Lysozyme Solution (Cat. No. 90082) to 200 µL of the EasyPep lysis buffer provided in the kit and proceed with the sample prep. Add 200 µL of the prepared lysis solution to 5 X 10E8 bacterial cells (E. coli cells) (OD600 equal to 1, corresponding to 1 X 10E8 CFUs). Lyse by pipetting the sample repeatedly and centrifuge at 16,000 x g for 5 mins. Alternatively, E. coli cells can be lysed in lysis buffer using bead beating or sonication instead of lysozyme. After lysis, dilute samples to 1 mg/mL using lysis buffer, proceed with the EasyPep protocol for reduction, alkylation, digestion, and clean up as described in the product manual.",-20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (-20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,Contents & Storage | Store below -20°C,,,"Contents & Storage
