≤1 month) or -80°C (≤2 months) to avoid loss of bioactivity and | or aliquot and store at -20°C.","Storage and Stability | Storage Condition | Samples to be used within 5 days may be stored at 4°C, otherwise samples must be | stored at -20°C (≤1 month) or -80°C (≤2 months) to avoid loss of bioactivity and | or aliquot and store at -20°C.",1,storage,"Page 1 [experimental]: On receipt entire assay kit should be stored at 4ºC for up to 6 months. | Page 1 [experimental]: On receipt entire assay kit should be stored at 4ºC for up to 6 months. (temperature: 4°C) | Page 1 [unclassified]: 4ºC (temperature: 4°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: 37°C incubator (temperature: 37°C) | Page 1 [unclassified]: Put unused solution back at 4°C. (temperature: 4°C) | Page 1 [unclassified]: warm it with 40°C water bath and mix it gently until the crystals have completely dissolved. (temperature: 40°C) | Page 1 [unclassified]: Serum: Coagulate the serum for 2 hour at room temperature or overnight at 4°C. (temperature: 4°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Plasma: Collect plasma using EDTA-Na2 as an anticoagulant. Centrifuge samples for 15 minutes at 1000×g at 2 - 8°C within 30 minutes of collection. (temperature: 2 - 8°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Cell culture supernatant: Centrifuge supernatant for 20 minutes to remove insoluble impurity and cell debris at 1000×g at 2 - 8°C. (temperature: 2 - 8°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: Other biological fluids: Centrifuge samples for 20 min at 1000×g at 4°C. (temperature: 4°C) | Page 1 [experimental]: incubate for 1.5 hours at 37ºC. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: plate and incubate at 37ºC for 60 min. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: Add 0.1 mL of SABC working solution into each well, cover the plate and incubate at 37ºC for 30 min. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: Add 90 μL of TMB substrate into each well, cover the plate and incubate at 37 ºC in dark (temperature: 37 °C)",PDF,https://content.abcam.com/content/dam/abcam/product/documents/289/ab289830/Human-Ovalbumin-OVA-ELISA-Kit-protocol-book-v1-ab289830%20(website).pdf
