mn volumes of buffer. | 4. Equilibrate the resin with 5-10 column volumes of buffer at a flow rate of ~1mL/minute for the 1mL column or | 5. For maximum binding, adjust the sample to the ionic strength and pH of the Binding Buffer by diluting it at least 1:1 | 7. Change the syringe and wash the resin with 5-10 column volumes of Binding Buffer. | Immediately adjust eluted fractions to physiological pH by adding 100µL of the Neutralization Buffer per 1mL of eluate. | Alternatively, add the Neutralization Buffer to the collection tube before eluting. | 9. Analyze the purified fractions directly by SDS-PAGE, or dialyze or desalt the sample into a buffer that is compatible | and re-equilibrate in Binding Buffer until the pH returns to the buffer value. | Dilute sample 1:1 with Binding Buffer or perform a | resin with the Binding Buffer | Sample being applied too fast for | Buffer | Desalt or dialyze eluted sample into suitable buffer | Additional Information Available on Our Website | Tech Tip #29: Degas buffers for use in affinity and gel filtration columns | Protein G IgG Binding Buffer, 3.75L",4-8°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (4-8°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,"Storage: Upon receipt store at 4-8°C. | Storage Solution | 10. For storage, wash the resin with five column volumes of water containing 0.02-0.05% sodium azide. Attach supplied | 11. For storage, wash the resin with five column volumes of water containing 0.02-0.05% sodium azide. Attach supplied | Tech Tip #43: Protein stability and storage | (III) USE OF THE PRODUCTS IN A MANNER FOR WHICH THEY WERE NOT DESIGNED, OR (IV) IMPROPER STORAGE AND HANDLING OF",,,"Storage: Upon receipt store at 4-8°C. | Storage Solution | 10. For storage, wash the resin with five column volumes of water containing 0.02-0.05% sodium azide. Attach supplied | 11. For storage, wash the resin with five column volumes of water containing 0.02-0.05% sodium azide. Attach s