ch as 1M phosphate or 1M Tris, (pH 7.5-9) | 3. Add 0.5mL of IP Buffer, centrifuge for 2-3 minutes at 2500 × g and discard supernatant. Repeat this step several times. | 5. Adjust eluate to physiological pH by adding ~10µL of the Neutralization Buffer per 100µL of eluate. The IP products | may be used directly for SDS-PAGE, or the buffer may be exchanged by dialysis or desalting column to one that is | Outgassing of buffers or sample | Degas buffers and remove air bubbles from column | Buffer | Try Gentle Ag/Ab Elution Buffer (see | suitable buffer | No antibody detected in any elution | Tech Tip #29: Degas buffers for use in affinity and gel filtration columns",4°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (4°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,"Storage: Upon receipt store product at 4°C. | 10. For storage, wash column with 5mL of 0.02% sodium azide. When approximately 3mL of solution remains, replace the | Tech Tip #43: Protein stability and storage | (III) USE OF THE PRODUCTS IN A MANNER FOR WHICH THEY WERE NOT DESIGNED, OR (IV) IMPROPER STORAGE AND HANDLING OF",,,"Storage: Upon receipt store product at 4°C. | 10. For storage, wash column with 5mL of 0.02% sodium azide. When approximately 3mL of solution remains, replace the | Tech Tip #43: Protein stability and storage | (III) USE OF THE PRODUCTS IN A MANNER FOR WHICH THEY WERE NOT DESIGNED, OR (IV) IMPROPER STORAGE AND HANDLING OF","Storage: Upon receipt store product at 4°C. | 10. For storage, wash column with 5mL of 0.02% sodium azide. When approximately 3mL of solution remains, replace the | Tech Tip #43: Protein stability and storage | (III) USE OF THE PRODUCTS IN A MANNER FOR WHICH THEY WERE NOT DESIGNED, OR (IV) IMPROPER STORAGE AND HANDLING OF","1, 3, 4",storage,Page 1 [shipping]: Storage: Upon receipt store product at 4°C. Product is shipped at ambient temperature. | Page 3 [unclassified]: Store columns upright at 4°C. (temperature: 4°C) | Page 3 [unclass