INSTRUCTIONS,protein G,P09471,Thermo Fisher,"Pierce Biotinylated Recombinant Protein G, 0.5mg, contains 1mM sodium citrate buffer at pH 6.8 | when reconstituted with 0.5mL of ultrapure water; any suitable buffer also may be used for | minimizes nonspecific binding. Typically, binding to Protein G is achieved using 0.1M sodium acetate buffer at pH 5.4; | Tris-buffered saline (TBS): 25mM Tris•HCl, 150mM NaCl; pH 7.2 (Product No. 28379) | Blocking Buffer: TBS containing 1-3% bovine serum albumin (Thermo Scientific Blocker BSA in TBS, Product No. | Note: A final concentration of 0.05% Tween®-20 Detergent in the blocking buffer often improves blocking; however, it | Coating buffer: 0.2M sodium bicarbonate, pH 9.4 (Product No. 28382) | Phosphate-buffered saline (PBS): 100mM sodium phosphate, 150mM sodium chloride; pH 7.0 (Product No. 28372) | Blocking buffer: PBS containing 1-3% bovine serum albumin (Blocker™ BSA in PBS, Product No. 37525) | Note: A final concentration of 0.05% Tween-20 Detergent in the blocking buffer often improves blocking; however, it is",6.8; 5.4; 7.2; 9.4; 7.0,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. Phosphate salts commonly help control pH and contribute ionic strength; exact effects depend on pH, concentration, and other ingredients. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. A detergent/surfactant may reduce surface adsorption or aggregation in some formulations; the exact purpose and compatibility depend on the specific ingredient and concentration. Bicarbonate can contribute to pH buffering, but its behaviour may depend on the solution's gas exposure and formulation. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Pierce Biotinylated Recombinant Protein G, 0.5mg, contains 1mM sodium citrate buffer at pH 6.8 | when reconstituted with 0.5mL of ultrapure water; any suitable buffer also may be used for | minimizes nonspecific binding. Typically, binding to Protein G is achieved using 0.1M sodium acetate buffer at pH 5.4; | Tris-buffered saline (TBS): 25mM Tris•HCl, 150mM NaCl; pH 7.2 (Product No. 28379) | Blocking Buffer: TBS containing 1-3% bovine serum albumin (Thermo Scientific Blocker BSA in TBS, Product No. | Note: A final concentration of 0.05% Tween®-20 Detergent in the blocking buffer often improves blocking; however, it | Coating buffer: 0.2M sodium bicarbonate, pH 9.4 (Product No. 28382) | Phosphate-buffered saline (PBS): 100mM sodium phosphate, 150mM sodium chloride; pH 7.0 (Product No. 28372) | Blocking buffer: PBS containing 1-3% bovine serum albumin (Blocker™ BSA in PBS, Product No. 37525) | Note: A final concentration of 0.05% Tween-20 Detergent in the blocking buffer often improves blocking; however, it is",-20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (-20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,,"Storage: Upon receipt store product at -20°C. | use of the Products in a manner for which they were not designed, or (iv) improper storage and handling of the Products.",when reconstituted with 0.5mL of ultrapure water; any suitable buffer also may be used for,,"when reconstituted with 0.5mL of ultrapure water; any suitable buffer also may be used for | Storage: Upon receipt store product at -20°C. | use of the Products in a manner for which they were not designed, or (iv) improper storage and handling of the Products.","when reconstituted with 0.5mL of ultrapure water; any suitable buffer also may be used for | Storage: Upon receipt store product at -20°C. | use of the Products in a manner for which they were not designed, or (iv) improper storage and handling of the Products.","1, 3",storage,Page 1 [shipping]: Storage: Upon receipt store product at -20°C. Product is shipped at ambient temperature. | Page 2 [unclassified]: at 37°C or overnight at 4°C. (temperature: 37°C; 4°C) | Page 2 [unclassified]: minutes at 37°C and aspirate. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: Add 150µL antibody solution and incubate for 1 hour at 37°C. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: (1µg/mL) to each well and incubate for 1 hour at 37°C. (temperature: 37°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: each well and incubate for 1-2 hours at 37°C. (temperature: 37°C),PDF,https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/manuals/MAN0011169_Pierce_Biotiny_Recomb_ProteinG_UG.pdf
