Cy5.5&reg; Conjugation Kit,recombinant human IgG,,Abcam,"Learn more about buffer compatibility, protein/secondary antibody conjugation and labelling | The purified antibody to be labeled should ideally be in 10-50mM amine-free buffer (e.g. MES, | MOPS, HEPES, PBS), pH range 6.5 to 8.5. If the buffer is more concentrated or outside this pH | Common non-buffering salts (e.g. sodium chloride), chelating agents (e.g. EDTA), and sugars | Avoid buffer components that are nucleophilic, as these may react with the kit chemicals. Primary | class (Note: Tris-based buffers should be avoided). If your buffer contains primary amines and/or",,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. HEPES is a pH buffer often used to help maintain solution pH; its presence alone does not establish protein stability or a storage temperature. EDTA chelates metal ions. This may matter if the protein requires metal cofactors or if metal-catalyzed reactions are relevant. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Learn more about buffer compatibility, protein/secondary antibody conjugation and labelling | The purified antibody to be labeled should ideally be in 10-50mM amine-free buffer (e.g. MES, | MOPS, HEPES, PBS), pH range 6.5 to 8.5. If the buffer is more concentrated or outside this pH | Common non-buffering salts (e.g. sodium chloride), chelating agents (e.g. EDTA), and sugars | Avoid buffer components that are nucleophilic, as these may react with the kit chemicals. Primary | class (Note: Tris-based buffers should be avoided). If your buffer contains primary amines and/or",4°C; -20°C,Cold chain indicated,Storage-context temperature at or below 8 °C was extracted (4°C; -20°C); verify the exact manufacturer instruction.,Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. A preservative may be desirable for long-term,Storage of conjugates | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. A preservative may be desirable for long-term | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. | storage. Other storage conditions may also be satisfactory. The best conditions for any particular | Storage instructions | Store at -20°C.,,,Storage of conjugates | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. A preservative may be desirable for long-term | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. | storage. Other storage conditions may also be satisfactory. The best conditions for any particular | Storage instructions | Store at -20°C.,Storage of conjugates | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. A preservative may be desirable for long-term | Storage at 4°C is recommended for any conjugate. | storage. Other storage conditions may also be satisfactory. The best conditions for any particular | Storage instructions | Store at -20°C.,2,storage,Page 2 [unclassified]: Replace cap on the vial and leave standing in the dark at room temperature (20-25°C) for 3 hours. (temperature: 20-25°C) | Page 2 [experimental]: Store at -20°C. Please refer to protocols.,PDF,https://doc.abcam.com/legacy-unpublished/datasheets/com/datasheet_102878.pdf
