Anti-VEGF Receptor 1 antibody [EPR21886-207] - BSA and Azide free (ab284963),vascular endothelial growth factor VEGF,,Abcam,"ab284963 is a BSA and Azide Free antibody supplied in an unconjugated format and it is suitable for sandwich ELISAs to quantify Human VEGF R1 (FLT1). The recommended pair for sandwich ELISA is: | Our carrier-free antibodies are typically supplied in a PBS-only formulation, purified and free of BSA, sodium azide and glycerol. This conjugation-ready format is designed for use with fluorochromes, metal isotopes, oligonucleotides, and enzymes, which makes them ideal for antibody labelling, functional and cell-based assays, flow-based assays (e.g. mass cytometry) and Multiplex Imaging applications. | Storage buffer | Constituents: PBS",,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Glycerol can act as a stabilizing co-solvent and may help reduce freezing-related damage, depending on its concentration and the protein. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. Sodium azide is commonly used as a preservative to limit microbial growth. It is hazardous and can affect downstream applications; follow the product safety sheet and assay compatibility guidance. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","ab284963 is a BSA and Azide Free antibody supplied in an unconjugated format and it is suitable for sandwich ELISAs to quantify Human VEGF R1 (FLT1). The recommended pair for sandwich ELISA is: | Our carrier-free antibodies are typically supplied in a PBS-only formulation, purified and free of BSA, sodium azide and glycerol. This conjugation-ready format is designed