Spillover to dairies
And now the poultry industry’s catastrophe has become the dairy industry’s problem, too. The virus’s 2024 appearance in Texas dairies was a surprise for flu experts: “The literature suggested that dairy cows don’t get influenza A’s,” says Pitesky — but, “as the joke goes, cows don’t read the literature.” Dairies were caught off guard,
without the guidelines and support systems
that exist for poultry. And by some reports, they’ve been
slow to adopt biosecurity measures","Kumar says Zoetis could turn stockpiled materials into ready-to-use vaccine in two months or less, depending on how close to finished form the vaccine is in storage. “We want to be ready,” he says.
