"Bispecific antibody: Structure, Formats, and Therapy",Penton base,P12538,Sino Biological,,,,,,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,", developed by MacroGenics, is a heterodimeric antibody composed of two polypeptide chains. Its production initiates with the linkage of the VH and VL domains from one antibody to the VL and VH domains of another via linkers, creating two scFv fragments. These scFv fragments are then co-expressed to facilitate proper VH-VL pairing and bispecific assembly. Additionally, cysteines are introduced at the C-termini of the two polypeptide chains to form interchain disulfide bonds, further enhancing the antibody stability.",,,,", developed by MacroGenics, is a heterodimeric antibody composed of two polypeptide chains. Its production initiates with the linkage of the VH and VL domains from one antibody to the VL and VH domains of another via linkers, creating two scFv fragments. These scFv fragments are then co-expressed to facilitate proper VH-VL pairing and bispecific assembly. Additionally, cysteines are introduced at the C-termini of the two polypeptide chains to form interchain disulfide bonds, further enhancing the antibody stability.
Bispecific Antibody Production
A number of strategies have been developed to generate bispecific antibodies. Three main production methods include chemical conjugation, quadroma technology, and genetic engineering. Among these,
genetic engineering
is currently
the most commonly used method",", developed by MacroGenics, is a heterodimeric antibody composed of two polypeptide chains. Its production initiates with the linkage of the VH and VL domains from one antibody to the VL and VH domains of another via linkers, creating two scFv fragments. These scFv fragments are then co-expressed to facilitate proper VH-VL pairing and bispecific assembly. Additionally, cysteines are introduced at the C-termini of the two polypeptide chains to form interchain disulfide bonds, further enhancing the antibody stability.
