"More typhoid conjugate vaccines, more impact",Protein VI,O60337,Gavi,"Having just one prequalified TCV, however, can create vulnerabilities for supply. A greater variety of products, manufacturers, and formulations will be beneficial for supply, affordability, and country choice. In December 2020, WHO granted | Typbar TCV is already making headway with its introductions in national immunization programs and in outbreak response. The WHO prequalification of TYPHIBEV and development of additional TCVs with different formulations will help improve TCV supply, lower costs, and provide for more country choice. With more options, formulations, and manufacturers, the TCV market will be diversified and fortified against supply bottlenecks. Furthermore, countries will have more freedom to choose which vaccine works best for their population and specific context.",,"The source reports a buffer/formulation, but its ingredients are not recognized by this simple interpretation rule set. Use the exact composition, pH, concentrations, and manufacturer's technical notes to interpret it. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Having just one prequalified TCV, however, can create vulnerabilities for supply. A greater variety of products, manufacturers, and formulations will be beneficial for supply, affordability, and country choice. In December 2020, WHO granted | Typbar TCV is already making headway with its introductions in national immunization programs and in outbreak response. The WHO prequalification of TYPHIBEV and development of additional TCVs with different formulations will help improve TCV supply, lower costs, and provide for more country choice. With more options, formulations, and manufacturers, the TCV market will be diversified and fortified against supply bottlenecks. Furthermore, countries will have more freedom to choose which vaccine works best for t