Getting beyond awareness: ‘learning by doing’ to reach zero-dose children in India",,storage,"[unclassified] <div> <div> <div> <div> <p>Every piece of equipment needs maintenance. That is just a fact of life. It may be routine maintenance, such as changing the oil in your car to prevent problems from occurring later on, or it may be the larger actions to repair or replace damaged parts. Sometimes you may even have to replace your car’s entire engine. Both types of maintenance, preventive and curative, are important to keep your car running as best as it can.</p> <p>Similarly, cold chain equipment (CCE) used to keep vaccines at an optimum temperature range of 2-8°C, needs regular preventive maintenance. This is absolutely necessary to keep the equipment functioning optimally, to maintain the vaccines quality and effectiveness against a disease, and to save lives.</p> <blockquote> | [unclassified] Similarly, cold chain equipment (CCE) used to keep vaccines at an optimum temperature range of 2-8°C, needs regular preventive maintenance. This is absolutely necessary to keep the equipment functioning optimally, to maintain the vaccines quality and effectiveness against a disease, and to save lives.",webpage,https://www.gavi.org/vaccineswork/keeping-cold-chain-cold-importance-maintenance
Product information for vaccines and cold chain equipment,interleukin 2 IL-2,,Gavi,"The CCE Technology Guide provides countries with guidance on selecting cold chain equipment that will meet the needs of the country’s immunisation programme. The CCE Technology Guide currently includes the following categories of equipment: Ice-lined refrigerators and freezers, solar direct drive refrigerators and freezers, freeze-free vaccine carriers, freeze-free cold boxes, long-term passive devices, temperature monitoring devices, and voltage stabilizers. Information is also included on equipment pricing, estimated operating costs, and product specifications.",,"The source reports a buffer/formulation, but its ingredients are not recognized by this simple interpretation rule set. Use the exact composition, pH, concentrations, and manufacturer's technical notes to interpret it. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","The CCE Technology Guide provides countries with guidance on selecting cold chain equipment that will meet the needs of the country’s immunisation programme. The CCE Technology Guide currently includes the following categories of equipment: Ice-lined refrigerators and freezers, solar direct drive refrigerators and freezers, freeze-free vaccine carriers, freeze-free cold boxes, long-term passive devices, temperature monitoring devices, and voltage stabilizers. Information is also included on equipment pricing, estimated operating costs, and product specifications.",,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,,,,,,,,storage_information_not_found,,webpage,https://www.gavi.org/our-work/market-shaping/product-information-vaccines-cold-chain-equipment
