Recombinant Proteins,myoglobin,P02144,Sino Biological,Carrier-free formulation: PBS buffer without BSA,,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Albumin may act as a carrier or stabilizer and can reduce non-specific loss of dilute proteins; confirm the role from the manufacturer's formulation notes. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.",Carrier-free formulation: PBS buffer without BSA,,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,"Strict stability evaluation ensuring batch-to-batch consistency | High purity, activity, stability, and low endotoxin | Designed for cell detection, high activity, stability, and specificity | include affinity chromatography, ion-exchange chromatography, and size-exclusion chromatography, which enable a stepwise increase in purity while maintaining the structural integrity and functional stability of the protein. The purification process typically involves two major stages: the initial removal of non-protein impurities, followed by the refined separation of the target protein from other protein components. Recombinant protein purification technologies are widely applied in the biopharmaceutical field, including the production of therapeutic proteins, vaccine antigens, and in vitro diagnostic reagents.",,,,"Strict stability evaluation ensuring batch-to-batch consistency
