"Protein subunit vaccines â What they are, and what they are notâ¯",protein A,P0DJI8,CEPI,,,,,,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,"Stability and a low risk of side effects are two of the main advantages of protein subunit vaccines. Because they contain no live components, they are also particularly suitable for pregnant women and people with compromised or weakened immune systems, such as elderly people or people living with HIV.",,,,"Stability and a low risk of side effects are two of the main advantages of protein subunit vaccines. Because they contain no live components, they are also particularly suitable for pregnant women and people with compromised or weakened immune systems, such as elderly people or people living with HIV.
However, protein subunit vaccines may not induce as strong or long-lasting immunity as some other types of vaccines, such as
mRNA
or
viral vector
vaccines, and may need to be boosted with additional doses to give better protection. To enhance the immune response, some protein subunit vaccines are combined with an adjuvantâa substance that boosts the vaccine's effectiveness.","Stability and a low risk of side effects are two of the main advantages of protein subunit vaccines. Because they contain no live components, they are also particularly suitable for pregnant women and people with compromised or weakened immune systems, such as elderly people or people living with HIV.
