Kit contents,protein G,P09471,Thermo Fisher,"Ab Binding & Washing Buffer | 16 mL | Washing Buffer | 28 mL | 30 mg/mL in phosphate buffered saline | buffers. | G beads, as well as buffers for | Washing Buffer to the magnetic beads from step 4 in “Prepare Dynabeads™ | Ab complex in 200 µL Ab Binding and Washing Buffer. Wash by gentle | Washing Buffer to prevent aggregation. | Buffer for each wash. Separate on the magnet between each wash, remove | Resuspend the magnetic bead-Ab-Ag complex in 100 µL Washing Buffer and | NuPAGE™ LDS Sample Buffer, then freeze the magnetic bead-Ab-Ag complex. | Buffer and NuPAGE Sample Reducing Agent. | a sample buffer of your choice (e.g. SDS sample buffer). Follow the recommended | temperatures and heating times for these buffers prior to gel loading. | This product contains Dynabeads™ Protein G for immunoprecipitation. | Cell Extraction Buffer | FNN0011 | NuPAGE™ LDS Sample Buffer | NP0007",,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Phosphate salts commonly help control pH and contribute ionic strength; exact effects depend on pH, concentration, and other ingredients. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. A detergent/surfactant may reduce surface adsorption or aggregation in some formulations; the exact purpose and compatibility depend on the specific ingredient and concentration. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Ab Binding & Washing Buffer | 16 mL | Washing Buffer | 28 mL | 30 mg/mL in phosphate buffered saline | buffers. | G beads, as well as buffers for | Washing Buffer to the magnetic beads from step 4 in “Prepare Dynabeads™ | Ab complex in 200 µL Ab Binding and Washing Buffer. Wash by gentle | Washing Buffer to prevent aggregation. | Buffer for each wash. Separate on the magnet between each wash, remove | Resuspend the magnetic bead-Ab-Ag complex in 100 µL Washing Buffer and | NuPAGE™ LDS Sample Buffer, then freeze the magnetic bead-Ab-Ag complex. | Buffer and NuPAGE Sample Reducing Agent. | a sample buffer of your choice (e.g. SDS sample buffer). Follow the recommended | temperatures and heating times for these buffers prior to gel loading. | This product contains Dynabeads™ Protein G for immunoprecipitation. | Cell Extraction Buffer | FNN0011 | NuPAGE™ LDS Sample Buffer | NP0007",,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,,Catalog No. 10007D Store at 2˚C to 8˚C,,,Catalog No. 10007D Store at 2˚C to 8˚C,Catalog No. 10007D Store at 2˚C to 8˚C,1,storage,"Page 1 [experimental]: protocol and elution at 2–8°C, to avoid protein complex dissociation and (temperature: 2-8°C) | Page 2 [unclassified]: Heat for 10 min at 70ºC. (temperature: 70°C)",PDF,https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/manuals/MAN0017348_dynabeads_protein_g_ip_kit_PI.pdf
