Protocol: Sandwich ELISA With Biotin-Streptavidin Detection (Colorimetric),streptavidin,P22629,Bio-Techne,"Custom Formulation Quotes | Phosphate Buffered Saline (PBS) | Coating Buffer: | Dissolve anhydrous 5.3 g Na | Phosphate Buffered Saline | Add the primary capture antibody to the Coating Buffer. If a working antibody concentration is not available, use the below table for recommended starting concentrations. The clonality of the antibody will impact the suitable concentration range.",,"PBS/phosphate-buffered saline generally provides pH buffering and salt conditions intended to keep the protein in an aqueous, near-physiological environment; the exact suitability depends on the product and concentration. Phosphate salts commonly help control pH and contribute ionic strength; exact effects depend on pH, concentration, and other ingredients. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Custom Formulation Quotes | Phosphate Buffered Saline (PBS) | Coating Buffer: | Dissolve anhydrous 5.3 g Na | Phosphate Buffered Saline | Add the primary capture antibody to the Coating Buffer. If a working antibody concentration is not available, use the below table for recommended starting concentrations. The clonality of the antibody will impact the suitable concentration range.",,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,,,,,,,,storage_information_not_found,[experimental] Dispense 100 µL of Capture Antibody Solution into the wells. Apply sealing tape to the top of the plate to prevent evaporation. Incubate the plate overnight at 4 °C. After incubation remove the tape and aspirate each well.,webpage,https://www.bio-techne.com/resources/protocols-troubleshooting/elisa-indirect-sandwich-protocol
