Vaccine stockpiles: a VaccinesWork guide,trypsin,P07477,Gavi,,,,,,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,"Their existence means that as soon as an outbreak of one of these diseases is confirmed and a request is made, countries can be vaccinating and protecting the unprotected within a matter of weeks.","Managed by the International Coordinating Group (ICG) on Vaccine Provision, these physical doses are housed in cold storage rooms around the world and can be accessed by any country that needs them, anywhere in the world, any time.",,,"Managed by the International Coordinating Group (ICG) on Vaccine Provision, these physical doses are housed in cold storage rooms around the world and can be accessed by any country that needs them, anywhere in the world, any time.
Their existence means that as soon as an outbreak of one of these diseases is confirmed and a request is made, countries can be vaccinating and protecting the unprotected within a matter of weeks.
To learn more about these stockpiles and how they work, read on below.
Everything you need to know about global emergency vaccine stockpiles
Q&A with Dr Allyson Russell, Gavi’s Senior Programme Manager for Outbreaks and Global Health Security
